      "content": "Interesting. I noticed you prioritized \"social support\" and \"home environment\" as heavy factors in your ranking. Can you elaborate on why those factors are considered more critical to clinical outcome than the actual physiological comorbidities? For example, shouldn't Patient C's age and lack of underlying diseases give him a significant physiological advantage over Patient B, despite his living situation?",
